LME changes (current): GlassOptics and liquid-glass.frag are simplified to a
single translucent tint layer (tint color, tint amount, panel opacity), procedural
grain, and geometry-based edge highlight/rim (SDF rounded box, edge gradient,
hairline/wide/broad/meniscus lighting). The shader does not sample desktop
background or wallpaper textures; blur comes only from the niri compositor.
Earlier LME modifications that added wallpaper snapshot backdrops, compositor-
yield blending, adaptive contrast, and related lens sampling have been removed.

Glass-on-glass nesting (Liquid Glass 2.0 G1): LME wires the walk into its own
GlassMaterial host. The level counts marked ancestor strata (GlassMaterial and
GlassPanel carry upstream's isGlassFill marker); the walk skips the carrier
(the child of a stratum that contains the walker), so a marked glass container
counts through its own embedded layer, never as itself. The level recomputes
only on tree events: parent changes and childrenChanged on watched ancestors,
coalesced with Qt.callLater and bounded to 48 levels. The domain stops at the
host window's content item. Nested optics attenuate rim and grain before values
are passed into the renderer.

